    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics has always been a comfort zone for me. As a student, I found it logical and structured, and even during my retirement, I've returned to it with delight. My children and I do occasional puzzles together. I've never been intimidated by its rules, though I admit I don’t always recall the finer details. It's a constant source of satisfaction.",
