    "How would you explain, step by step, how to find the stationary points of an equation y=f(x)?": "You take the derivative of the function, f'(x). Then, you solve for x when f'(x) equals zero. These x-values are the stationary points. Plug them back into the original function to find the y-values. These are the points where the function stops increasing or decreasing.",
